00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:47.240
the reduction of angle of attack.

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:50.560
So this is the envelope and for the stall resistance, I think

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:53.000
there are a lot of factors that go into this.

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:57.520
The first one will be the pressure is like how much

00:17:57.520 --> 00:18:00.920
pressure do you get before you you actually go into the stall?

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:03.680
And if you have the, the glider is really hard to stall.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.040
That deforms a lot, gives you a lot of pressure before you stall

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:08.240
that it's going to be really hard to stall by accident,

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:12.360
especially if you, let's say get a collapse or private, then it's

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.560
a lot easier to stall. But if from the beginning you

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:18.800
have that super direct and clear stall point, then it gives you

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:21.920
that extra safety margin. On the other side of the

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:25.800
spectrum, it's a bit more tricky and let's say new in, in the

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:30.400
latest development of the design lately we've started to use more

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:32.880
and more airfoil with a pitch up tendency.

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:37.000
And so that pitch up tendency means that let's say you take

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.000
the glider and you cut all the lines off.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:42.880
And if your glider wants to, basically if the nose wants to

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:46.320
pitch up and, and go towards the flight towards the sky, then

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:48.040
that that is the pitch up tendency.

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:52.240
But then on the other side of of the spectrum, if you have, if

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:54.840
you let the glider fly on its own and if it immediately jumps

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:57.080
into a collapse, that's the pitch down tendency.

00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:00.680
And in the past, most gliders had that pitch down tendency.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.480
Just a second. So the aerofoil, let's say if

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:08.200
this is the aerofoil in stable terms, any successful aerofoil

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:11.000
is supposed to sink at one metre per second according to parallel

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.880
design. So the pitch up tendency, you

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:16.120
mean like how is that designed? Is that designed to make the one

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:19.320
metre per second lower? No, no, no, it doesn't.

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:23.480
It doesn't affect the performance significantly, not

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:26.120
in like calm conditions. It's about reacting to

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.840
turbulence. It's not about like your steady

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:33.040
state flight. And basically the the pitch of

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:37.880
tendency is that it behaves in a way that if the ankle of attack

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:41.760
reduces, then the centre of lift goes forward towards the nose or

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:45.560
even beyond the nose. And so that puts all of the load

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:47.360
on the A lines. And then your Air Force just

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:51.120
wants to pitch up and go against the reduction of the Gulf

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:54.120
attack. And the outcome is like when you

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:58.920
fly the pitch down tendency will more be, I mean it depends a lot

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:01.360
on the glider. Some deform will deform more, we

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:04.320
communicate more. But basically when you fly the

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:10.440
pitch down tendency, the if you have a down downwash gas like

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:13.960
reduction Armageddon attack, then the profile wants to go

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:16.280
with the collapse. And so there is a tendency to

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:20.960
just collapse completely and brutally and you don't really

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:25.280
have time to react. And if you have more pitch up

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:28.520
tendency, then basically the, the profile when the lines go

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:31.480
slag because you're losing lift the the profile wants to go

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:33.400
against the collapse. And So what you feel in the

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:36.680
hardness instead of like boom, everything going, you feel that

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:38.960
you're falling because you're losing tension.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.920
And this is, will give the pilot more time to react.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:46.720
And the more you have this pitch up tendency, the more you have

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:51.960
this collapse resistance, the easier it will be for the pilot

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:54.880
to have time to react and the more it will be for the pilot to

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:58.040
basically fly safely at high speed through turbulence.

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:02.120
And this is kind of a new trend in the design that we didn't

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.320
have in the past for several reasons.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:09.160
The first one is that basically if you have a profile that goes

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:11.720
against the reduction of angle of attack, this is a profile

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:15.000
that will go against the reduction of angle of attack

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.280
that you're looking for when you want to accelerate.

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:20.480
So that's a profile that goes against acceleration.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:26.080
And so it has been a challenge to still get good top speed with

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:30.440
pitch up tendency, high strong pitch up tendency, especially if

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:33.720
your range is limited like on the CCC for instance, where we

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:37.040
have a speed range that is limited to 14 centimetre, which

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:41.200
limits strongly the amount of reflex or pitch up tendency that

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.520
you can implement in your airfoot.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:47.520
Then the other factor which is the biggest limitation in

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:51.600
practice will be the collapse. If you think about parakeets for

