00:40:37.680 --> 00:40:39.640
be order 1 and projected aspect order.

00:40:39.680 --> 00:40:43.240
What's the difference? Between what's the do you feel

00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:45.000
actual? Because flat aspect ratio to me

00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:47.200
is just a number and that's not how your wing is.

00:40:47.280 --> 00:40:50.200
It's just so projected is the only reference point.

00:40:50.200 --> 00:40:53.360
Is that correct? Not really because also

00:40:53.360 --> 00:40:55.520
projected it really depends on how you measure.

00:40:56.400 --> 00:40:58.640
And I think from different software and different brands we

00:40:58.640 --> 00:41:00.840
