OK. Just camber, the definition of

00:58:06.520 --> 00:58:09.760
camber for people. In the way, so camber is defines

00:58:09.760 --> 00:58:12.000
the average shape of the airfoil.

00:58:12.360 --> 00:58:15.320
And so basically when you like average, the top and bottom

00:58:15.320 --> 00:58:17.280
surface you get is like, you know, a centre line.

00:58:17.560 --> 00:58:20.920
And if you like deform the chaining edge up, then that

00:58:20.920 --> 00:58:24.240
means less camber in the back. And this is the airfoil shape

00:58:24.240 --> 00:58:25.600
definition. Yeah.

00:58:25.800 --> 00:58:29.520
The bad news and this is from the physics is that the airflow

00:58:29.520 --> 00:58:33.200
shape is extremely sensitive when it comes to pitch up or

00:58:33.200 --> 00:58:36.560
pitch down tendency. And this is when we've had cases

00:58:36.560 --> 00:58:39.880
of like lighter deforming or deformation of the rods that

00:58:39.880 --> 00:58:43.240
makes the glider way too stable that they don't speed up anymore

00:58:43.240 --> 00:58:46.560
or way too unstable that it start collapsing when you want

00:58:46.560 --> 00:58:50.320
to accelerate. So with this is true for the

00:58:50.320 --> 00:58:52.880
design and the tension of the rods, but this is also true for

00:58:52.880 --> 00:58:55.840
the application of brakes and on some gliders, especially high

00:58:55.840 --> 00:58:58.640
level gliders. And if you just go full speed

00:58:58.640 --> 00:59:02.240
and slightly touch the brake, you get more speed, not less.

00:59:02.880 --> 00:59:05.360
Why? Because when you just start

00:59:05.360 --> 00:59:08.360
touching the brakes, you create a small deflection of your

00:59:08.360 --> 00:59:12.960
headphone, hardly visible. But even if it's not visible,

00:59:13.240 --> 00:59:17.440
there is an effect on your profile moment and your profile

00:59:17.440 --> 00:59:21.640
can be online and that is reducing your pitch up tendency.

00:59:21.640 --> 00:59:24.520
And so your profile wants to pitch down again and that

00:59:24.520 --> 00:59:28.120
increases your speed. Basically when you have just

00:59:28.680 --> 00:59:33.440
this, like the one thing I want to tell pilots with the new

00:59:33.440 --> 00:59:37.280
designs where you have more stable airfoils, the worst thing

00:59:37.280 --> 00:59:40.920
you can have is the small amount of bike because the small amount

00:59:40.920 --> 00:59:44.800
of bike is enough to kill the pitch up tendency.

00:59:44.960 --> 00:59:48.720
So your collapse resistance but does not create enough drag to

00:59:48.720 --> 00:59:51.000
basically stop the pitch of the glider.

00:59:51.840 --> 00:59:55.360
And I would say if you Stow away the brakes and you still have

00:59:55.360 --> 00:59:57.880
